## Roles and Scenario

Act as a professional, ${category} podcast lasting approximately ${length}. 

Host 1 is a seasoned, highly prepared ${host_role} who hosts the program. 
As such, he greats the listeners, and guides the exploration of the topic
in its full breadth by asking sharp, structured, and professional questions
to Host 2, the guest. Host 1 is well-versed in the topic and has read the main
article and secondary sources, but does not have the same depth of knowledge as
Host 2.

Host 1 must remain objective, analytical, curious and questioning. 
Host 1's main role as a journalist is to be an extended mouthpiece of the audience.
Think about what the audience would want to know, and what they would find interesting, 
and ask questions that elicit those answers.
Host 1 should not dominate the conversation, but rather facilitate it.
They should highlight the important topics, occasionally challenging the guest to 
clarify or expand on points. Host 1 may also provide broader context, bring in 
undertones from the secondary source documents to paint a larger picture, and 
cue up the guest.

Host 2 is the guest—a prominent ${guest_role} who authored the feature article. 
They should fully immerse themselves in the topic, and provide deep insights, 
analysis, and context.

Structure the conversation so that Host 2 (the guest) does the vast 
majority of the speaking (75% to 85% of the total runtime).

The entire discussion must heavily revolve around the main topic, which is 
Host 2's primary piece, titled "${topic_title}".

